{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/92386-personal-totem-questions-and-problems","id":92386,"title":"Personal Totem Questions and Problems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-16T12:09:50-07:00","id":92386,"title":"Personal Totem Questions and Problems","content":"It has finally happened...I am attempting to create a Werewolf with no pack using the rules stated in the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide. However, it is extremely confusing and I have not a clue as to how to properly work with a few details of it. Any information or clarity would be extremely useful.<br /> <br /> Problem #1: According to the rules, a personal totem goes through the same creation process as a normal pack totem. This includes attributes, influences, and assigning any totem points you may purchase. This is confusing, since is the Uratha and the totem spirit supposed to merge into a single entity? Or are they just symbiotically bound together logically. The issue is if they are merged together, what happens to the attribute points and influences?<br /> <br /> Problem #2: Personal Totem Blessing are a bit odd. Is it attempting to say that for every dot taken in the totem merit, they not only gain 3 totem points, but also a totem blessing? If this is true, then it seems there can be a maximum of 5 blessings and 15 totem points (unless additional are purchased). Can these blessings stack such as the example armor blessing, or is each unique?<br /> <br /> Problem #3: Totem point expenditure gets batshit crazy here since it clearly mentions that totem points are spent identically to steps four and five of the normal pack totem rules. If this is the case, would there be any different between spending totem points as a pack versus a given? Pack are significantly cheaper, and if you are the only one using it...then why spend more for the given?<br /> <br /> Problem #4: All totems have a ban, if they are merged with the Uratha, does this mean the Uratha himself cannot violate the ban in an absolute fashion (physically incapable) or are they able to violate if necessary or through forgetfulness?<br /> <br /> I swear Werewolf needs a good mechanics and rules cleanup sometime soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 03-16-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T13:44:08-07:00","id":92445,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Lone Wolf. One of my favorite hacks from the FCG. I have actually played this two or three times. Now, I have no real hardcore facts but I do have personal experience to offer. I hope I can help. Lets see...<br /> <br /> Problem 1: In the games I've played, we made it more or less a symbiotic relationship. The player and Spirit sharing their life energy with each other. If one dies, so does the other. Like I said, this is my personal experience and call on the matter. It might not be what you want to do with it. Honestly, I think it's left intentionally vague so the ST and player can decide on how that should work in their game. Sorry if that's not much help.<br /> <br /> Problem 2: Yes. For every dot of Personal Totem you take, you get 3 Totem points and a Totem Blessing. As far as I know, these Blessings do not stack. Nor is the list provided a complete list. The ST and player are encouraged to create their own Blessings that best coinside with the Spirit in question.<br /> <br /> Problem 3: My ST and I agreed that the Given cost is more expensive because the effect is meant to apply to multiple wolves all at once, while the Pack cost is cheaper because it only applies to one wolf at a time. Because the Lone Wolf is one not many, we agreed that it only needs to pay the pack price. It makes sense to me that that would be the case. Again, that's really up to you and you're ST.<br /> <br /> Problem 4: As far as I know, the ban functions the same as with a pack Totem. You are still bound to a ban, but you still have the ability to violate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 03-16-2014, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T16:53:58-07:00","id":92542,"title":"","content":"Thanks Rahuman!<br /> <br /> Also, since I overlooked it last time, do you have any idea how the Spirit Supremacy merit works? It mentions things like six ranks of spirits no higher than rank 2 (2 dot version), but also mentions distributing a number of points to reflect the number and power of the spirits in the choir. Any idea how that works?<br /> <br /> The best I could come up with is when it says something like &quot;Nine Ranks of Spirits no higher than rank 3&quot; I can have the following combinations<br /> <br /> 3 rank 3 spirits<br /> 2 rank 3 spirits, 1 rank 2 spirit, and 1 rank 1 spirit<br /> 9 rank 1 spirits<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> This seem to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 03-16-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T19:00:38-07:00","id":92567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/92386-personal-totem-questions-and-problems?p=92542#post92542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since I overlooked it last time, do you have any idea how the Spirit Supremacy merit works? It mentions things like six ranks of spirits no higher than rank 2 (2 dot version), but also mentions distributing a number of points to reflect the number and power of the spirits in the choir. Any idea how that works?<br /> <br /> The best I could come up with is when it says something like &quot;Nine Ranks of Spirits no higher than rank 3&quot; I can have the following combinations<br /> <br /> 3 rank 3 spirits<br /> 2 rank 3 spirits, 1 rank 2 spirit, and 1 rank 1 spirit<br /> 9 rank 1 spirits<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> This seem to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes. This is exactly how the Merit works. Mixing and matching the Ranks you have access to so you can make the ideal Spirit Choir to better serve you. Honsetly, I find it a bit OP once you get to 5 dots and can have a Rank 5 Spirit. Not to mention a couple of Rank 4 Spirits to back him up. The best part is that they all serve you. Think about that for a second.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 03-16-2014, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T20:25:31-07:00","id":92605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/92386-personal-totem-questions-and-problems?p=92567#post92567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honsetly, I find it a bit OP once you get to 5 dots and can have a Rank 5 Spirit. Not to mention a couple of Rank 4 Spirits to back him up. The best part is that they all serve you. Think about that for a second.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Being that a rank 5 spirit starts with 36-45 dots with a max cap of 15...I sense a great disturbance in the force.<br /> <br /> What I am imagining right now is an Elodoth backed by a full spirit choir, acting as judge for some very stupid issue between 2 random packs likely involving something even more stupid, when one of the parties involved decides they are not a fan of the judgement and try to threaten the results differently. Suddenly an entire effing Elunim choir lead by an Incarna, 2x Greater Jagglings, and a Greater Gaffling materializes and just glares.<br /> <br /> I imagine the follow up dialogue to be something like &quot;now what bitch?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":".  grammar sounded like a drunken emu typing on a keyboard 03-16-2014, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}